heetMetalDocument","suffix":".psm","expect":{"manual":"The size depends on which side the thickness went; we compare it by hand."}},{"id":"S09a","scripted":false,"why_not":"Contour flange on an existing edge: no working call on Solid Edge 2026 in ordered sheet metal (our Solid Edge test PC, 2026-11-23, own hidden instance, 8 probe runs). ContourFlanges.Add has no edge argument (the edge comes from the profile start and the optional chained edge set); Add, AddEx and Add3 (with the key-point arguments) return E_FAIL with the chained edge set missing, as a typed Edge[] or as the single edge, and RPC_E_SERVERFAULT with an Object[]; tried with extent to end of edge (14) and finite (13), both projection sides, bend relief square/none and corner relief none/closed from FlangeFeatureConstants, explicit neutral factor, close-corner and mitre arguments, and the open up-20-then-10 profile on the end plane at x = 0, on a parallel plane, on a plane normal to the edge, starting at z = 0 or 2, with the wall on either side of the edge and the lip toward +Y or -Y, with and without the profile check; AddSync and AddSyncEx are the synchronous-mode calls (E_POINTER or the same fault in ordered mode). The same profile builds as a base contour flange (Models.AddBaseContourFlange, used for S08), so the failure is the edge-attached call; two stacked flanges would give the C shape but not a contour flange, so the recipe is not built that way","progid":"SolidEdge.SheetMetalDocument","suffix":".psm","expect":{"bbox":[[0,null,0],[100,null,null]],"manual":"The flange shape depends on the edge options; we compare it by hand."}},{"id":"S09b","scripted":false,"why_not":"Contour flange on an existing edge: no working call on Solid Edge 2026 in ordered sheet metal (our Solid Edge test PC, 2026-11-23, own hidden instance, 8 probe runs). ContourFlanges.Add has no edge argument (the edge comes from the profile start and the optional chained edge set); Add, AddEx and Add3 (with the key-point arguments) 